# Engineering Practices

## Before Changing Anything

1. Inspect the existing repo (layout, `app.py`, `db/`, `services/`, `ui/`, seeds, README).
2. Reuse and extend existing code; do **not** unnecessarily overwrite or restructure working work.
3. Do **not** make architectural changes without a clear reason tied to the Design Document or an explicit user request.

## Target Layout (when implementing)

```text
app.py
db/          # database.py, schema.sql, seed.py
services/    # room, status, assignment, user services
ui/          # dashboard, cr_panel, teacher_panel, admin_panel
data/        # room_status.db
requirements.txt
README.md
```

Keep business logic in `services/`, not buried only in Streamlit widgets, so migration later stays feasible.

## Coding Rules

- Keep implementation **simple and maintainable**; prefer clarity over cleverness.
- Separate **UI**, **business logic**, and **database** operations where practical.
- Reuse helpers/services instead of duplicating queries or validation.
- Keep dependencies **minimal** (Streamlit + stdlib SQLite unless the user asks otherwise).
- After meaningful changes: run/seed the app and verify the affected workflow (assign → update → view → revoke).
- Do not expand into out-of-scope production tech (see design-source-of-truth rule).

## Success Criteria (Prototype)

Local seed → Teacher assigns CR → CR updates status → Student sees it + history → revoke assignment → CR blocked. Prove the product loop, not production infrastructure.
